{"title":"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4(very_risky_and_very_stupid)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4(very risky and very stupid)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Headache)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Headache)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Induction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Induction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A strictly increasing sequence of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087594ea26fa196b8e61bc20a36228270dc695f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" /> has the property that for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the subsequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a1c72c346e3a95d0eaeb0f0848f15cf4a2cffe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56331f2f2110a9332540a65efa78eed8abe2a049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/5579b99a2778d61c48c54c194a1cc8c518de938b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> is geometric and the subsequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56331f2f2110a9332540a65efa78eed8abe2a049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/5579b99a2778d61c48c54c194a1cc8c518de938b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821ad83f9eebe4db5872d149d6f53647b959ddf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> is arithmetic. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6ebd12838ca71023c0d05fe8087797ed3385581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13} = 2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first create a similar sequence where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b02a491e6fc8db3a577b344b1a53b7a8e77e0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/3/2a3df751ea79fb4a5832cf4dd090dbed2884df86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />. Continuing the sequence,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/379a1d7d69c4081e01f0805a4429ba0111b0f954.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1, 2,4,6,9,12,16,20,25,30,36,42,49,\\cdots\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Here we can see a pattern; every second term (starting from the first) is a square, and every second term (starting from the third) is the end of a geometric sequence. This can be proven by induction. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22dc606a9481cf00726a3b766573a0fcb470b7a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> would also need to be the end of a geometric sequence (divisible by a square). We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea42c71f0fe69a63703523300b5e972dc1bf7eee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^5 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 7$\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, so the squares that would fit in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f4215c50c3e48737000cc4b9230577fda74d20c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fcc33a7c840ca476cc3df92991ac6edc1acb78d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee19f2230cc721282aa8253c8d9b7e5ff8ffbe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2=9$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9584bdb500d49089d884caad5e9f4484b6267bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12caade2b7b1b61e63b329b5e87a8bc9b3b3772f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2 \\cdot 3^2 = 36$\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e39307752064628fc10c3a0aebe4226c866152d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4 \\cdot 3^2 = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />. By simple inspection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is the only plausible square, since the other squares in the sequence don't have enough elements before them to go all the way back to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> while still staying as positive integers. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fe2cda44fcf75467de6752491e264c9c9160124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13}=2016=14\\cdot 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd1a978b3bd512f463061496e439da1f2129427c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=14\\cdot 36=\\fbox{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>~IYN~\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd1990ea279ef93b36b0678f0013fa8581fe3d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/3/db3ff3c6011732ef7ba7d42aba70c73f4f240fad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 = ka$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />, the sequence becomes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d330b959a2c009ea109c7edcc9acab3bce663e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a, ka, k^2a, k(2k-1)a, (2k-1)^2a, (2k-1)(3k-2)a, (3k-2)^2a, \\cdots\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"19\" />\nand so forth, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e341058280447574963173b0f0ba96148f17978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2n+1} = (nk-(n-1))^2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"19\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d5bb7e72bbca9a71670e44ec65b61b75a244d18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13} = (6k-5)^2a = 2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"19\" />. Keep in mind, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> need not be an integer, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/574077fa8aab6185a88f2396d6dcfb06b45de6be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2a, (k+1)^2a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"19\" /> etc. does. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/599c4a0dd0699d098be68d6d4ca7193c77fc2352.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016 = 2^5*3^2*7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" />, so only the squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a33d264defd7f802524b8d73da8a619657cf1f4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 4, 9, 16, 36,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> are possible for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/39966c91b26129518ed8cf42d1027d4afba77917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6k-5)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"19\" />. But when that is anything other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/521851f3266f4c3b0b6d86cd0e5600cc47fcbdca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2a$\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" /> is not an integer. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/6/a7656b744bfa3516b1de4ed26f8aea8a93cec5c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2016/2^2 = 504$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Thanks for reading, Rowechen Zhong.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Instead of setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> equal to something and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> equal to something, note that it is rather easier to set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f665d3b06d994ad9d43d38cb69e1ff0f0e29f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6e0b5d83cca87b8791af45c7af8a088120d0d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460c0745ef850dba234f8561e83f08f696c257be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=xy,a_4=y(2y-x),a_5=(2y-x)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"310\" height=\"21\" /> and so on until you reached <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60e8e6163db53317e9107ced71d57f1982605a53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13}=(6y-5x)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"21\" /> (Or simply notice the pattern), so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c248ad6af8c26b50496e2b97919d2d49b2226d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6y-5x=\\sqrt{2016}=12\\sqrt{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"214\" height=\"23\" />. Note that since each of the terms has degree 2 so if you multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b4f6a1c096ea750ff28732f86571789d6cf895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> you multiply each term by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> so each term is still a integer if the terms are already integers before you multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b4f6a1c096ea750ff28732f86571789d6cf895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, so let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/642f59be83b83fd698ae4f505e06013b416fa899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{14}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"77\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b23e19fb4f522e5eac5199c9dc726253db12ad56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{14}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"73\" height=\"39\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd166c6de9b5542db472388518edb3155ac03a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6z-5w=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. Then, for the sequence to be strictly increasing positive integers we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3576b4802c2f464d6cee9a4a16df8ba49769a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(w,z)=(6,7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f062a8b9036e1f0a22fb1a4624e8ef68322091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=6\\sqrt{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db7832cf334e941d6476be2023b734e6c731298c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=x^2=6^2 \\cdot 14=\\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"196\" height=\"25\" />~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001\" title=\"Ddk001\">Ddk001</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4.28very_risky_and_very_stupid.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4(very_risky_and_very_stupid)\">Solution 4(very risky and very stupid)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4(very risky and very stupid)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The thirteenth term of the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, which makes that fourteenth term of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/1805241b8376d5865eb10d18001febde24b55d9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097078d8a659ca86b7e2e2591a9ef82d731e52b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{\\text{th}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebae4e07cf267b1dc4b44281cb535ebde9efb97d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2016+r)^2}{2016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"39\" />. We note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer so that means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd80b54adf6d284d5a062e785e874bb3b0facde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{r^2}{2016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"39\" /> is an integer. Thus, we assume the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c7116bbc884d2cf49e25754864ae00d9c42d2d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. We bash all the way back to the first term and get our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47b99edd8b63c0f040ab7bf194a4409d72e44d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-Pleaseletmewin\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab52e5ed5d0c922fe7cd856bf01eb34ad4ce2d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k-1}=s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b9f92ce163af6710d6d12efc941e6656cbf4d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k}=sr \\Longrightarrow a_{2k+1}=sr^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"197\" height=\"21\" />. Continuing on, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d23399ea4df7c54818c2b9476df03b9cdf317b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k+2}=sr(r-1)+sr^2=sr(2r-1) \\Longrightarrow a_{2k+3}=sr^2(\\frac{2r-1}{r})^2=s(2r-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"598\" height=\"38\" />. Moreover, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/0548792d8483b2e22108861035972bd02ee7d262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k+4}=s(2r-1)(r-1)+s(2r-1)^2=s(2r-1)(3r-2) \\Longrightarrow a_{2k+5}=s(2r-1)^2(\\frac{3r-2}{2r-1})^2=s(3r-2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"816\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>It is clear now that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/72071c3e916191303f8af55de27cd8f467f2f85c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k+2c}=s(cr-(c-1))((c+1)r-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"294\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530a5a08465adaecbad5c4c284290741fe1bbc29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k+2c-1}=s(cr-(c-1))^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"21\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb76404ee79952dcc555464b061509299789b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e1a6c9d94993062b7a62d57860fc1b51da0995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13}=s(6r-5)^2=2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"21\" />. The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a3ca36a0680597a5550a3cabbc590ef7bdcd6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016=2^5\\cdot3^2\\cdot7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"17\" /> so we look for perfect squares.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645c4a8d88199eff6d8e17421bd8632c2f1f8f5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r-5\\equiv (6r-5)^2\\equiv 1\\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"251\" height=\"21\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/10822ad5ffc70bda604096decb2af0863bc5e4d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\omega+5}{6}=r \\Longrightarrow 6\\mid{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not an integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is rational, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e6092fa15e9a30a4c576783a2c189ea5f9e3f89d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\mid{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" />. This forces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e24ffb03771bce8508d56e1e988e0e5c4faf38c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=2\\cdot3^2\\cdot7\\cdot{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"17\" />. Assuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4426b549d4c1d6e979d9e025e708f60474a992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6r-5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" /> is an integer, it can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065d0462782004d830c2bfbda340ff333d710f37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^x$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/554588b8be9f32e0380c6be3f4b08ab4d253ac25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in{1,2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dcab5156c7aeeaf6cbb7dcc07088dd66d34c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r-5=2^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/1453c4479720ca434dcba155f159757a287d8d7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{7}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45362677b5915ba4f68e1eed1ba8d966a125c68a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r-5=2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f59385a2c0c9e13b9400204711b531b1dddae851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />. Note that the latter cannot work since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f192a3a64ee17db2c8b9612f83dd361f47e77997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k+1}=s(\\frac{9}{4}) \\Longrightarrow 4\\mid{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"175\" height=\"38\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/8057f65415527695373d4e7b5406427ca4e087aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=1 \\Longrightarrow s=2\\cdot3^2\\cdot7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"185\" height=\"17\" /> in this scenario. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df2280c1710e1fb941e8ddbe256db67204669560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{7}{6} \\Longrightarrow s=\\frac{2016}{2^2}=504$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"212\" height=\"38\" />. Plugging back <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bf9b85424a1d340ca84b3852743da97b9495d83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=s=\\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Magnetoninja\">Magnetoninja</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Headache.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Headache)\">Solution 6 (Headache)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Headache)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bash all the way from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bf184fbf5bcf37304889e9177bce38fb75f8205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13}=2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> to get to the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19aee569fa8eba4d21b282efe4132ab2ba794399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1\\left(\\frac{6a_2}{a_1}-5\\right)^2=2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"178\" height=\"48\" /> and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd964f4285b214282713823f63d889d8f50ab5dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=2\\sqrt{14a_1}+\\frac{5}{6}a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"38\" /> (direct consequence). Notice that from the two equations we can deduce that:\n</p><p>1) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca2435f13ddd560e82479c9da7a95f019f0496a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1\\mid2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p><p>2) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/55462d6fc8f0b1150e7f3f57e742d5ca944b7950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\mid a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />, and\n</p><p>3) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d24b778ff796e110f3b849609979537f8f5687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{a_1}{14}}\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"76\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/428a7386345855ce1d6bfdf19dcd5a3e482c7414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016=2^5\\cdot3^2\\cdot7=14(2^4\\cdot 3^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"234\" height=\"21\" />, the only possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> that satisfy the conditions are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb4795bbf9125d08b3ddc9fbe238166da3bb450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$126$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f385769245cc3c249ec34e15661c168bfb48e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$504$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> itself. Obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be a correct answer choice (from AIME rules), and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/6/ac69b26566d2b90136ea0a0688fe7a573cd051a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=126$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6bbef23c3eadadb85663a36f29096e61a2b048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3\\not\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47b99edd8b63c0f040ab7bf194a4409d72e44d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> is the solution.\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7c565cebd94b1989e66da1aa987e404b31354c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{11} = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e68e6a700aeea638558ee97f81b1977512c028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{12} = xr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a293977b126b9e0bf0e49fcbb41020260409c388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13} = xr^2 = 2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />. Note, in order to alternate between arithmetic and geometric sequences, you would want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to be as small as possible so our sequence is always positive as stated in the question. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fbd6c635ec2a9c8b23bc9082ba8b0c18a563af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016 = 2^5 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"129\" height=\"15\" />, the smallest ratio, r, (which must be greater than 1 as the sequence is strictly increasing) must satisfy that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b077547a9105e1c255d99bd1281e9034173da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_12 = \\frac{2016}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e91736811f142d7b228b5d7b853d4ee28cbfe4b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_11 = \\frac{2016}{r^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> are both integers. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b8be31d9e21e92918f42cfaa7b324766d507b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> can at min be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1da2bef2956e3b2e0af4f4b1298566f6eca036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{2^2 \\cdot 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"45\" height=\"34\" />. To minimize this we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e921f405977229521ee7bc3cf5dc0fe3b62cdca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/7/307379d1011f9ed2bd67c03cb1a3a86172859830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{12}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />. Doing this and working backwards, we get the sequence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db984e9ed41f304cd1de08c2d0e58004c0186631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 504 a_2 = 588 a_3 = 686 a_4 = 784 a_5 = 896 a_6 = 1008 a_7 = 1134 a_8 = 1260 a_9 = 1400 a_{10} = 1540 a_{11} = 1694 a_{12} = 1848 a_{13} = 2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"992\" height=\"17\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a210a3884dab680647897690a15e0f02ef27094c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = \\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"82\" height=\"25\" />\n~Sid-darth-vater\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Induction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Induction)\">Solution 8 (Induction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Induction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b72ec24905d982811e3680754c36f6868ff64bef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=a,a_2=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />, we know that for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />,\n\\begin{align*}\na_{2k}^{2}&amp;=a_{2k-1}\\cdot a_{2k+1}\\\\\n2a_{2k+1}&amp;=a_{2k}+a_{2k+2}\n\\end{align*}\nComputing some following terms, we have\n\\begin{align*}\na_3&amp;=\\frac{b^2}{a}\\\\\na_4&amp;=\\frac{b(2b-a)}{a}\\\\\na_5&amp;=\\frac{(2b-a)^2}{a}\\\\\na_6&amp;=\\frac{(2b-a)(3b-2a)}{a}\n\\end{align*}\nWe see a pattern for the 2 sequences consisting of the odd terms and even terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f83edd3c0baaa2971621cff4f1d0fe25f895b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_{n}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" />. We proceed with induction.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30bc3e22ba410312637a3baefa2f572d918f5936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k=a+(k-1)d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc993dd11667abaf1ec918cf29ecba2675ecd893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=b-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. We attempt to prove the following:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/7683fb19bb3883eb1e11c1407fe923525827e4e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{2k-1}=\\frac{c_{k}^{2}}{a}, \\qquad a_{2k}=\\frac{c_{k}c_{k+1}}{a}\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"39\" />\nThis is obviously true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Assuming this statement is true for a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18c143fea49df4c82f12a86375008fa94c4a42ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{2k+1}=\\frac{a_{2k}^{2}}{a_{2k-1}}=\\frac{(\\frac{c_{k}c_{k+1}}{a})^2}{\\frac{c_{k}^2}{a}}=\\frac{c_{k+1}^2}{a}\\]\" width=\"263\" height=\"51\" />\nAlso, using the rule of the arithmetic subsequence, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebe59f10e5564a6cbfa368f400a76865ae797daf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{2k+2}=2a_{2k+1}-a_{2k}=\\frac{c_{k+1}(2c_{k+1}-c_{k})}{a}\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"38\" />\nWe see that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be1d6031809d358fd22ea2c115dcdfd2a5862ecf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2c_{k+1}-c_k=2a+2kd-a-(k-1)d=a+(k+1)d=c_{k+2}\\]\" width=\"469\" height=\"18\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c0d52395fe20c405dd5c9df6c950a498ca69cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2k+2}=\\frac{c_{k+1}c_{k+2}}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"34\" />, our induction hypothesis is hence proven.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56bda508179f520ff2c7dad27b96af4815c4ca14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\mid c_{k}^2 \\iff a \\mid d^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bf184fbf5bcf37304889e9177bce38fb75f8205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13}=2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00aa05738ceec274f978591f752279c57a8ec983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a+6d)^2}{a}=2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"41\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1f852aa5fc08e3f13d57e55c2bbfda604d772e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=a+6d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />. This follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b471ca63cbf732b35d713639c7b6a0d18f2c89f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=\\frac{k^2}{2016}\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"39\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b30103a9261473178ef846506d01021905c4b22f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016=2^5\\cdot 3^2\\cdot 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"17\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece5b48d02f1ccbdf4583ab54597258d75c6498c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=168m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />, this follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbde34d9813b2fe63c2eced96cf510742af9ae42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=14m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4ef7b1300255c0e5d7c2aedf220f984e2e099e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6d=k-a=168m-14m^2\\implies d=\\frac{7}{3}m(12-m)\\]\" width=\"397\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> needs to be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b9b1a2b66489773875594f2a4667db6743b992f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=3j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />, we find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94d7ee65cab799da10936d0847e76b552b2300f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d=7j(12-3j)\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />\nThe cases for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e9918ec1e4c4b4104586dc0f9715676af0eca2f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j=1,2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" /> gives the solutions\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/b/aeb1391e61679afcefb4fdc5af7e0c7b74cb9171.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a, d)=(126,63),(504,84),(1134,63)\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"18\" />\nNote that only the second ordered-pair suffices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31c406d5efb96214a4ce2e2f09863235d0fd6686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\mid d^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, the solution is hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01f53e6e3feb7c85b270ba2aa56e670bbb333fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}=a=\\boxed{504}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"116\" height=\"25\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fVRHaPE88Cg\">https://youtu.be/fVRHaPE88Cg</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I\" title=\"2016 AIME I\">2016 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203849\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.086 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 905/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1788/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 110/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 29746/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.227      1 -total\n 58.96%    7.209      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.35%    4.811      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14841:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017203849 and revision id 292826. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}